from the Chicago skyline follow the  southbound tracks for half an hour and  you will arrive at the latest  battleground in the us-china trade war  in this gleaming new hundred million  dollar manufacturing plant China's CR RC  is building the first of 800 passenger  rail cars for Chicago's elevated trains  but Congress is now considering banning  the company from making trains here  unfortunately  we along with some others are the  collateral damage of a much bigger issue  the trade war and the geopolitical  strife and issues that are going on  between China and the US these wires  meet the next potential casualties of  the trade war we want to be a part of  something special for Chicago and for  that to be taken away from us would be  disheartening and unfortunately we would  just have to find somewhere else to work  CR RC has 300 workers at our plant in  Massachusetts and plans to double the 90  here in Chicago but China has a major  image problem here with Donald Trump  sparking an economic battle with the  world's second largest economy the bill  to blacklist China from passenger rail  projects that receive federal funding  which is virtually all of them has drawn  support from both parties since Pullman  built its last car in 1968 no American  manufacturer makes passenger rail cars  the trade war launched by the Trump  administration aims in part at  increasing business and employment here  in the United States but mistrust  between the two countries is so great  that the u.s. seems intent on punishing  China even if it means also hurting jobs  and manufacturing here at home some  members of Congress fear China's growing  economic dominance and the national  security threat posed by what they claim  could be listening devices embedded in  rail cars critics call them spy trains  CRR C calls that ridiculous  CR RC  is not doing that when CRC builds the  rail cars and delivers them to the  Transit Authority CTA takes full control  of the rail cars economists say 